  "issue_title_or_body_excerpt": "## Evidence \u2014 2026-10-07 local audit\n\nDo Again's native watchdog was merged into `main` (`6afd748`), and PR #8 (`a02b997`) passed 17/17 CI jobs and was merged. However, **main branch success is not installed-runtime success**.\n\n- `jobpipe`: installed `service/liveness.py`, configuration explicitly sets `continuous=true`, `report_stalls=true`, and current `do-again status` exposes `liveness_state=working`.\n- `Sonary`: installed runtime has no `service/liveness.py`, project configuration has no `continuous=true`, and `do-again status` exposes no liveness state; the project has been doing long-running recording/DAW development tasks.\n- `do-again` itself: installed runtime has no `service/liveness.py`, configuration has no continuous mode, no liveness status. Its source checkout was fast-forwarded to merged `main`; copied service remains older code.\n- Both jobpipe and Sonary were actively processing tasks at inspection. **Do not restart/replace their daemon, policy, browser, or execution worktree while a request is claimed/running.**\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Develop safe, version-aware, in-flight-safe upgrade flow: checks outstanding requests/claims, execution PIDs and terminal receipts; waits or explicitly defers service replacement and restarts. Preserve project configuration, current ChatGPT chat ownership/rollover records, outbox, and resume state. Refuse unsafe upgrade, never silently cancel operations or replay unconfirmed effects.\n2. Enable intentional continuous development goals for Do Again and Sonary where authorized; no auto-continuation of an explicitly completed, paused, or one-off goal. Preserve jobpipe setting and track it separately.\n3. Use `do-again status` to distinguish idle-with-goal, queued delivery, running/claimed, authenticating, waiting for CI, paused, completed, recovering, and stalled. A green daemon alone must not pass the health check.\n4. Live end-to-end fault-injection/soak for each project: idle ChatGPT after succeeded receipt; queued delivery; long-running claim; crash/auth/network failure; bounded recovery with no duplicate side effects. Prove at least one deliberate stall produces safe progress or visible incident/issue without manual chat prompting.\n5. Surface notifications to user when a project cannot recover, deduplicated sanitized issues, and a no-secrets local incident trace. Avoid issue spam across restarts.\n6. Only after safe rollout, validate running runtime has the expected source hash/feature imports, required config, daemon state, and recent progress evidence.\n\n**Status:** Source merged/CI green, rollout + live fault-injection evidence missing. Do not mark resolved solely on passing CI. Related root-cause issue: #9."
